This distribution is a downstream fork of Tencent/BrowserSkill
<https://github.com/Tencent/BrowserSkill>, which is licensed under the MIT
License. The upstream copyright notice and the upstream license terms are
retained in LICENSE and apply to all code inherited from upstream.

Modifications and additions made in this fork are distributed under the same
MIT License. Additions that do not exist upstream include:

- `bsk invoke` (raw JSON-RPC passthrough), `bsk templates` (Profile Templates)
  and `bsk completion`
- `bsk browsers close`, `bsk browsers --browser-id`, and user-scope tab
  management (`tab list|create|select --browser-id`, `tab observe`)
- opt-in profile account id reporting (used to tell browser profiles apart)
- `--since last_action` relative cursor for `console` and `network`
- editable instance smart labels

Upstream remote/server mode — `crates/bsk-cli/src/daemon/remote/**` and
`apps/extension/src/transport/remote-*` — is carried in the tree so the
repository stays mergeable with upstream. It is **not supported** by this
distribution: it is not enabled by default, it is not documented as a
capability, and its future upstream changes are not adopted. The supported and
default mode is loopback only.

See docs/UPSTREAM_SYNC.md for the sync policy, the ported and not-ported lists,
and the current divergence from upstream.
